+# Proposed F2/F3 approval packet — not authorized or executed
+
+This packet is reversible preparation under the [existing owner approval](../ext-secrets-1-erasure-authority-2026-10-20/OWNER-APPROVAL.md). Choosing the component-internal AWS reference implementation grants no provisioning, key creation, expenditure, deployment, physical experiment, Agents consumption, Live/cohort attempt, register change or availability declaration. All installed identities remain null in `approval-packet.json`.
+
+The proposed maximum expenditure is **USD 100 total**, including retained storage and cleanup, for the exact seven native keys, one current-authority table, two archive buckets and two control instances below. A current itemized provider quote and budget alarm must fit that ceiling before an approval can authorize execution. Unknown account, placement, independent owners/trust and retention sign-off prevent execution; they are explicitly listed rather than invented.
+
+| Proposed resource | Fixed cap and proposed purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `custody-f2f3-small-source`, `custody-f2f3-small-candidate`, `custody-f2f3-small-successor` | Three generated single-region `AWS_KMS` symmetric erasure epochs; the candidate is the sole permitted tainted generation. No imported, replicated, exportable or custom-store key. |
+| `custody-f2f3-large-source`, `custody-f2f3-large-successor` | Two more epochs for the complete 1,000-target lane. **Five epochs total**, including every abandoned candidate. |
+| `custody-f2f3-small-kek-protector`, `custody-f2f3-large-kek-protector` | Exactly two distinct native KEK protectors. Tenant KEK encrypted bytes remain separate from every erasure epoch. |
+| `hexalith-custody-f2f3-20261023-current` | One DynamoDB current-authority table; no global-table replicas, restore/recreate permission or TTL. Pin actual table ID and ARN at independent enrollment. |
+| `hexalith-custody-f2f3-20261023-checkpoints`, `hexalith-custody-f2f3-20261023-originals` | Two versioned S3 archives with expected owner, exact enrolled version and compliance retention. Proposed names remain subject to actual ownership/availability; substitution requires updating this packet before approval. Combined experiment storage ceiling 1 GiB. |
+| `custody-f2f3-executor`, `custody-f2f3-observer` | Exactly two control instances, proposed Linux hosts in distinct approved failure/administration domains, independent from the app restore cut. Enrollment is an independently held identity, not a third control instance. |
+
+The only tenant IDs proposed are `custody-f2f3-small` and `custody-f2f3-large`. One original joint schedule owns both lanes; no new destructive identity or replacement attempt after uncertainty. The small lane contains one held root, one selected root and one independent survivor; the large lane owns one sorted complete 1,000-target manifest. One physical cycle per tenant, no target sharding or per-target deletion.
+
+The proposed retention minimum is 120 days for new immutable objects/journals, with review and extension at least 30 days before the current lock expires and **no expiry while any referenced batch, outcome, backup or public verification remains live**. Authority heads/allocation exclusions have no TTL. Numeric retention is a proposal, not accepted OA-6 disposition. Original local and independently archived request/result/attempt/recovery journals are append-only and never removed by cleanup. If the budget cannot fund required retention, do not admit the experiment; a cost alarm never authorizes evidence deletion.
+
+The separate approval must bind actual account/region, independent executor/observer/enrollment identities and public SPKI fingerprints; authority/table/bucket/epoch/KEK IDs; independent host/site/restore boundaries; exact component, daprd, SDK and kernel artifacts; network/UDS ACLs; installed closure/sanitation/termination verifiers; measured admission/completion reserve; vendor assurance and private IAM policies. Runtime permissions exclude resource creation, authority restore/recreate, object deletion, cancellation of key deletion, replacement epoch creation and direct application/provider access.
+
+The approved executor would retain the complete exact requests before any send; enroll actual authority/genesis outside restored apps; prove hold/reserve ordering; freeze/drain/copy/retire/adopt; schedule the sole source cut; inject duplicate/cancellation/lost acknowledgement/SDK/sidecar/component/UDS faults under the original identities; and collect final independently signed native, holder, survivor and restore evidence. A schedule acknowledgement or missing key never completes the experiment. See `f2-f3-schedule.json` for the ordered stop conditions.
+
+Allow six active engineering days plus genuine deletion/evidence wait. Earliest proposed start is the first business day after exact approval and all installations; no date is accepted here. After 15 business days from an approved native start without final evidence, retain `Blocked/Unknown` and request scoped continuation. There is no completion SLA and no automatic retry, extra candidate, extra cycle, or cap reset.
+
+Cleanup is separately observed: stop/terminate enrolled producers after buffer reconciliation, preserve exact journals/originals/public verifiers and exclusions, verify no target revival from old copies and independent survivor recovery, and remove only explicitly approved synthetic resources after their retention/reference obligations permit it. Every cleanup action and unresolved resource remains in the original journal. Total surviving-authority loss remains fail-closed; it never authorizes restoration or self-enrollment.
+
+Approval request, once all missing identities and quote are filled and hash-bound: approve only the exact `approval-packet.json` and `f2-f3-schedule.json` hashes, the USD 100 ceiling, named accountable owners, retention obligations and independently observed cleanup. **No approval is assumed by preparing this packet.**
